        <headline>Marine Weather Statement issued August 14 at 8:38PM EDT by NWS Charleston SC</headline>
        <description>The areas affected include...
Waters from South Santee River to Edisto Beach SC out 20 NM...

* At 838 PM EDT, Doppler radar indicated strong thunderstorms,
capable of producing winds to around 30 knots. These strong
thunderstorms were located along a line from 7 NM west of Cape
Romain Reef to over Bulls Bay, moving southeast at 10 knots.

Locations impacted include...
Jimmy Leland Tug, Hector Reef, Cape Romain Reef and Bulls Bay.
</description>
        <instruction>Report severe weather to the Coast Guard or nearest law enforcement
agency. They will relay your report to the National Weather Service
office.</instruction>
