        <senderName>NWS North Platte NE</senderName>
        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued August 14 at 9:28PM MDT by NWS North Platte NE</headline>
        <description>At 927 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 13
miles southeast of Rushville, moving northeast at 30 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and penny size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is
possible.

Locations impacted include...
Gordon, Clinton, Lone Butte, Highway 27 crossing the Niobrara River,
Highway 250 crossing the Niobrara River, Rock Hill, and Intersection
of Highway 27 and Mills Road.

This includes the following highways...
Highway 20 between mile markers 93 and 106.
Highway 250 between mile markers 31 and 46.
</description>
        <instruction>If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.</instruction>
        <web>http://www.weather.gov</web>
        <parameter>
            <valueName>AWIPSidentifier</valueName>
            <value>SPSLBF</value>
        </parameter>
        <parameter>
