        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued August 14 at 8:28PM MST by NWS Phoenix AZ</headline>
        <description>At 828 PM MST, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near
Scottsdale Airport, or near Paradise Valley. This thunderstorm was
nearly stationary.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects.

Locations impacted include...
Phoenix, Scottsdale, Fountain Hills, Paradise Valley, Papago Park,
Piestewa Peak Park, Downtown Scottsdale, Scottsdale Airport,
Camelback Mountain, North Mountain Park, and Desert Ridge
Marketplace.

This includes the following highways...
AZ Route 51 between mile markers 5 and 15.
AZ Route 101 between mile markers 31 and 48.
</description>
